  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Making Tax work for women BURKINA Faso</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this &quot;Making tax work for women Burkina Faso project, the external impact targeted is the existence of a binding measure for the respect of GRB principles in Burkina.
The decision-maker we want to influence is the Prime Minister(ministry responsible for the budget et and national assembly of the transition) of the government, as he is the key player in the macroeconomic framework in the gender budgeting stages. The strategy used will be advocacy by the CSO platform
At the end of the second phase, the success of our work will be as follows: a plea is made to the Prime Minister for the introduction of a measure of constraint for the respect of the principles of GRB
A strong and influential platform of Burkinabe women&apos;s organisations with a better understanding of macroeconomic policy and its impact on gender and a watchdog role on government action exists,&#xA0; and is connected with other strong women&apos;s organisations in the sub-region and around the world.</narrative>
  </description>
